{
  "id": "merge-two-sorted-lists",
  "title": "Merge Two Sorted Lists",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "categories": ["linked-list"],
  "descriptionMd": "You get the heads of two singly linked lists, `list1` and `list2`, and each one is already sorted in non-decreasing order.\n\nCombine them into **one sorted linked list** by relinking the existing nodes, and return the head of the result.\n\n**Example 1**\n\n```\nlist1 = [1, 2, 4], list2 = [1, 3, 4]\n→ [1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 4]\n```\n\n**Example 2**\n\n```\nlist1 = [], list2 = [0]\n→ [0]\n```\nIf one list is empty, the answer is simply the other list.\n\n**Follow-up:** can you solve it both iteratively and recursively?",
  "constraints": ["0 ≤ length of each list ≤ 500", "-100 ≤ Node.val ≤ 100", "Both lists are sorted in non-decreasing order."],
  "hints": ["At every step, only the two current front nodes are candidates for the next position.", "A placeholder node in front of the result saves you from special-casing the first pick."],
  "signature": {
    "functionName": "mergeTwoLists",
    "params": [{ "name": "list1", "type": "ListNode" }, { "name": "list2", "type": "ListNode" }],
    "returns": "ListNode"
  },
  "comparator": "exact",
